tail":"en"},{"id":"viewport","label":"Responsive viewport (zoom not disabled)","pass":true,"detail":"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"},{"id":"open-graph","label":"Open Graph tags (5/6)","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"twitter-card","label":"Twitter card metadata","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"open-social","label":"Open social presence (Mastodon/Bluesky) linked","pass":false,"detail":""}],"passed":8,"total":11,"social":[],"og":{"title":"Planning Phase - Center for Visual Structural Expertise for Resilience (C-ViSER)","description":"The last update is from 2024.The integration of machine learning innovations into the practice of structural engineering offers opportunities to enhance the safety, resilience, and environmental sustainability of the United States' built environment and support the growth of the U.S. economy. The engineering and architecture services sector is critical to the nation, accounting for 2.8% of the U.S. GDP, and bears substantial responsibility for approximately 37% of the global carbon emissions.Structural design and evaluation, pivotal in this sector, serve as the bridge between architectural vision and the realization of construction or maintenance projects. The early stages of design, assessment, and analysis crucially impact a project's outcome and operational life cycle. Despite this importance, the in-depth exploration of alternative approaches or solutions is typically time and cost-prohibitive, limiting the potential for optimizing project resilience, safety, sustainability, and functionality. Enhancing the productivity, capabilities, and collaborations of structural engineers through artificial intelligence advancements can address these limitations.The envisioned Center for Visual Structural Expertise for Resilience (ViSER) will focus on developing foundational machine learning innovations to enhance design and management practices in the built environment. To realize and implement these innovations in practice, the Center will cultivate a diverse workforce skilled in both structural engineering and artificial intelligence. This approach not only fosters scientific advancement but also promotes inclusive development within the structural engineering field and will catalyze wide-reaching benefits for the built environment, economic growth, and societal well-being.","url":"/centers/center-for-visual-structural-expertise-for-resilience-viser/","image":"/assets/images/twittercard.png","siteName":null,"type":"article"},"resilience":{"checks":[{"id":"pwa-https","label":"HTTPS (required for service workers)","status":"pass","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-visual-structural-expertise-for-resilience-viser/","why":"HTTPS is required for service workers and most install prompts."},{"id":"pwa-manifest","label":"Web app manifest declared","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-visual-structural-expertise-for-resilience-viser/","why":"A web app manifest is required for installability and controls how the app appears when launched."},{"id":"pwa-service-worker","label":"Service worker registered","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-visual-structural-expertise-for-resilience-viser/","why":"A service worker is what makes offline access, caching, and background sync possible."},{"id":"pwa-theme-color","label":"Theme color declared","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-visual-structural-expertise-for-resilience-viser/","why":"Theme color controls the browser chrome/status-bar color when the site is installed or bookmarked."},{"id":"pwa-apple-touch-icon","label":"Apple touch icon (iOS/bookmark icon)","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-visual-structural-expertise-for-resilience-viser/","why":"iOS uses this icon for home-screen bookmarks and \"Add to Home Screen\" — without it the icon falls back to a screenshot."},{"id":"manifest-parsed","label":"Manifest fetched and parsed successfully","status":"n/a","evidence":"No manifest declared","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-visual-structural-expertise-for-resilience-viser/","why":"A manifest that fails to parse cannot drive installability or launch behavior even if the link is present."},{"id":"manifest-maskable-icon","label":"Manifest declares a maskable icon","status":"n/a","evidence":"No manifest declared","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-visual-structural-expertise-for-resilience-viser/","why":"A maskable icon lets the OS safely crop/mask the app icon on different device shapes without clipping content."},{"id":"sw-active","label":"Service worker is active (not just registered)","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-visual-structural-expertise-for-resilience-viser/","why":"An active service worker (not just registered) is what actually intercepts requests and serves cached content."},{"id":"sw-controlling","label":"Service worker controls this page load","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-visual-structural-expertise-for-resilience-viser/","why":"A controlling service worker means THIS page load is being served/intercepted, not just a future one."},{"id":"installable","label":"Meets basic installability criteria","status":"fail","evidence":"no readable web app manifest; no service worker registered","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-visual-structural-expertise-for-resilience-viser/","why":"Determines whether the browser can realistically offer \"Add to Home Screen\" / install, based on manifest + service worker + HTTPS together."}],"manifest":null,"serviceWorker":{"registered":false,"active":false,"installing":false,"waiting":false,"controllingThisPage":false}}}}